# Task: Build "Evergreen", a TTL / state-archival keeper for Soroban contracts

You are building an open-source project end to end. I will not be available for questions, so make reasonable decisions yourself and record each one in `docs/DECISIONS.md` (decision, alternatives, reason). Work in phases, commit after each meaningful step, and keep the repo in a working state at every commit.

## 1. Background and goal
Soroban contract data, contract instances and contract code entries have a TTL (time to live) measured in ledgers. If nobody extends it, entries are archived and the contract can stop working until the entries are restored. Most teams handle this with ad-hoc scripts or forget it entirely.

Evergreen watches deployed contracts, warns before entries expire, and automatically extends (or restores) TTLs within strict fee and budget limits. It also provides a CI check and a small dashboard. The project must be clean and well documented enough that an external maintainer would trust it and outside contributors could pick up issues easily.

**Verify every Stellar/Soroban detail against current official documentation before relying on it** (state archival, `ExtendFootprintTTL`, `RestoreFootprint`, RPC methods, fee/resource handling, network limits on maximum TTL, ledger timing). Do not rely on memory for protocol numbers. If docs and your assumptions conflict, follow the docs and note it in DECISIONS.md. Never invent APIs; if unsure, read the SDK source or docs.

